{
  "id": "ch-derivatives",
  "chapterNumber": "2",
  "title": {
    "en": "Derivatives",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The derivative is the <span style=\"color:var(--indigo); font-weight:600\">first question of calculus</span> made precise: the instantaneous rate of change of \\( f \\), equivalently the slope of the tangent line to its graph.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 2.1 — The derivative",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>The derivative of \\( f \\) at \\( x \\) is the limit of slopes of secant lines:</p>\\[ f'(x)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}, \\]<p>when this limit exists. It is also written \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx} \\) or \\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}f(x) \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "As \\( h\\to 0 \\), the secant through \\( \\big(x,f(x)\\big) \\) and \\( \\big(x+h,f(x+h)\\big) \\) pivots into the tangent. Watch it happen — drag the point of tangency and the slope readout below updates live.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
